<title>FINLAND: Kesko thinks EU will approve Tuko sale.</title>
<headline>Kesko thinks EU will approve Tuko sale.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wholesaler and retailer Kesko Oy said on Thursday it expected the EU Commission to let it keep the Anttila department stores and Rautia hardware stores and approve its sale of the rest of former rival Tuko.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope and believe that Anttila and Rautia could remain (part of Kesko),&quot; Kesko board member Matti Halmesmaki told a news conference.</p>
</text>
